                    <occupation/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin encounters this Hunter only at Joseph Johnson's dinners which makes it likely that he is related (father, brother?)
  to Rowland Hunter, Johnson's grandnephew. Rowland had a brother Roger to whom Johnson left £100.
  There is a possibility that it may be John Hunter (<title>DNB</title>; 1737–1821), naval officer and colonial governor as the rank and dates make it possible.  Although note
  promotion to rear admiral on 2 October 1807, and vice-admiral on 31 July 1810 which, if the same Hunter, Godiwn does not acknowledge.</p>
                        <p>For other Hunter entries see the discussion in <persName key="HUN03"/>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
